      "content": "I'm sorry, but I don't understand the reference to \"pressure-loving goblins\" or \"shape-shifting goblins.\" This is a technical oceanographic inquiry for a research paper, and those metaphors are irrelevant to the physics of the TEOS-10 equation. \n\nPlease disregard the analogies and provide a rigorous, purely mathematical and physical explanation of the interaction between the pressure-dependent terms and the thermal expansion coefficient. I need the actual scientific reasoning regarding the density gradient.",
